.TH MACOSX-CROSS-LLD 1 "September 2026" "macosx-cross @MACOSX_CROSS_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
macosx-cross-lld \- invoke ld64.lld for Apple cross-linking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B macosx-cross-lld
.RB [ \-\-macosx-sdk =VERSION ]
.RB [ \-\-target =TARGET ]
.RB [ \-\-arch =ARCH ]
.RB [ \-\-lld =PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.RI [ ld64.lld-arguments ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B macosx-cross-lld
is a wrapper around
.BR ld64.lld (1)
for linking Mach-O binaries for Apple platforms from a non-Apple host.

The wrapper selects an Apple SDK, target triple, architecture, deployment
target, library search paths, and platform information before invoking
.B ld64.lld .

All arguments not recognized as wrapper options are passed directly to
.B ld64.lld .

The wrapper automatically supplies several linker arguments when they have
not already been specified, including the SDK system library root,
architecture, and platform version.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-macosx-sdk =VERSION
Select the macOS, iOS, or related Apple SDK version.

The SDK is expected at:

.RS
.nf
@MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/VERSION
.fi
.RE

For example:

.RS
.nf
--macosx-sdk=10.9
--macosx-sdk=14.5
--macosx-sdk=15.5
.fi
.RE

If this option is omitted, the default
.B MacOSX.sdk
directory is used.

.TP
.BR \-\-target =TARGET
Select the Apple target triple.

Examples include:

.RS
.nf
x86_64-apple-darwin
arm64-apple-darwin
arm64-apple-ios
x86_64-apple-ios
arm64-apple-ios-macabi
x86_64-apple-ios-macabi
.fi
.RE

The target is required.

.TP
.BR \-\-arch =ARCH
Explicitly select the Mach-O architecture.

If omitted, the architecture is inferred from the target.

Supported examples include:

.RS
.nf
x86_64
arm64
arm64e
arm
i386
.fi
.RE

.TP
.BR \-\-lld =PATH
Explicitly select the
.B ld64.lld
executable.

For example:

.RS
.nf
--lld=/opt/llvm/bin/ld64.lld
.fi
.RE

If omitted, the wrapper searches for
.B ld64.lld-19
and
.BR ld64.lld ,
including standard
.I /usr/bin
and
.I /bin
locations.

.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Display usage information and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-
Stop processing wrapper options.

All following arguments are passed directly to
.BR ld64.lld .
.SH TARGET PLATFORMS
The target determines the Apple platform used for linking.

.TP
.B macOS
Targets matching:

.RS
.nf
*-apple-darwin*
.fi
.RE

use the macOS SDK and
.B MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET .

.TP
.B iOS
Targets matching:

.RS
.nf
*-apple-ios*
.fi
.RE

use iOS SDK metadata and
.B IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET .

.TP
.B Mac Catalyst
Targets matching:

.RS
.nf
*-apple-ios-macabi*
.fi
.RE

use the Catalyst platform and
.B IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET .
.SH AUTOMATIC LINKER OPTIONS
Unless explicitly supplied by the caller, the wrapper adds:

.TP
.BR \-syslibroot " " SDK
Sets the SDK as the linker system library root.

.TP
.BR \-arch " " ARCH
Selects the Mach-O architecture inferred from or specified by
.BR \-\-arch .

.TP
.BR \-platform_version " " PLATFORM " " DEPLOYMENT " " SDK_VERSION
Specifies the Apple platform version information required by
.BR ld64.lld .

The platform is one of:

.RS
.nf
macos
ios
mac-catalyst
.fi
.RE
.SH LIBRARY SEARCH PATHS
The wrapper constructs library and framework search paths from the selected
SDK and its metadata.

Standard SDK paths include:

.RS
.nf
<SDK>/usr/lib
<SDK>/usr/lib/system
<SDK>/System/Library/Frameworks
<SDK>/System/Library/PrivateFrameworks
<SDK>/Library/Frameworks
<SDK>/Library/PrivateFrameworks
.fi
.RE

SDK paths are passed to the linker using
.BR \-L
or
.BR \-F ,
depending on their type.

Absolute Unix SDK paths such as
.I /usr/lib
and
.I /System/Library/Frameworks
are interpreted relative to the selected SDK where appropriate.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MACOSX_ROOT
Installation root used by the configured wrapper.

The installed wrapper normally uses:

.RS
.nf
@MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B MACOSX_SDK_VERSION
Default SDK version when
.B --macosx-sdk
is not supplied.

.TP
.B MACOSX_TARGET
Default target triple when
.B --target
is not supplied.

.TP
.B MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
Deployment target for macOS.

If unset, the selected SDK version is used.

.TP
.B IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
Deployment target for iOS and Mac Catalyst.

If unset, the selected SDK version is used.

.TP
.B LIBRARY_SEARCH_PATHS
Additional library search paths for macOS targets.

Paths are added to the linker search path when they exist.

.TP
.B LIBRARY_IOS_SEARCH_PATHS
Additional library search paths for iOS and Catalyst targets.

.TP
.B IOS_UNZIPPERED_TWIN_PREFIX_PATH
Optional iOS twin SDK prefix.

The wrapper can add its
.I usr/lib
and
.I System/Library/Frameworks
directories to the linker search paths.

.TP
.B SYSTEM_FRAMEWORK_SEARCH_PATHS
Additional framework search path passed to the linker using
.BR \-F .
.SH SDK METADATA
The selected SDK may contain:

.RS
.nf
<SDK>/.metadata
.fi
.RE

This file is sourced as a shell script and may define:

.RS
.nf
SDK_VERSION
MACOSX_SDK_ARCHS
MACOSX_SDK_IOS_ARCHS
MACOSX_SDK_IOSMAC_ARCHS
LIBRARY_SEARCH_PATHS
LIBRARY_IOS_SEARCH_PATHS
IOS_UNZIPPERED_TWIN_PREFIX_PATH
.fi
.RE

The metadata is used to determine SDK information and additional search
paths.
.SH LD64.LLD SELECTION
If
.B --lld
is not specified, the wrapper searches for
.B ld64.lld
in the following order:

.RS
.nf
ld64.lld-19
ld64.lld
/usr/bin/ld64.lld-19
/usr/bin/ld64.lld
/bin/ld64.lld-19
/bin/ld64.lld
.fi
.RE

The first executable found is used.
.SH ARGUMENT PASSING
Arguments not recognized by the wrapper are preserved and passed unchanged
to
.BR ld64.lld .

For example:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-lld \\
    --macosx-sdk=14.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    main.o -lSystem -o test
.fi
.RE

is equivalent to invoking
.B ld64.lld
with the wrapper-generated SDK, architecture, platform, and search-path
arguments in addition to:

.RS
.nf
main.o -lSystem -o test
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Link an x86_64 macOS executable:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-lld \\
    --macosx-sdk=10.9 \\
    --target=x86_64-apple-darwin \\
    main.o -o test
.fi
.RE

Link an arm64 macOS executable:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-lld \\
    --macosx-sdk=14.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    main.o -lSystem -o test
.fi
.RE

Link an arm64 iOS executable:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-lld \\
    --macosx-sdk=14.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-ios \\
    main.o -o test
.fi
.RE

Link an arm64 Mac Catalyst executable:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-lld \\
    --macosx-sdk=14.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-ios-macabi \\
    main.o -o test
.fi
.RE

Explicitly select the architecture:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-lld \\
    --macosx-sdk=14.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    --arch=arm64 \\
    main.o -o test
.fi
.RE

Use a specific linker:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-lld \\
    --lld=/opt/llvm/bin/ld64.lld \\
    --macosx-sdk=15.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    main.o -o test
.fi
.RE

Pass additional linker options:

.RS
.nf
macosx-cross-lld \\
    --macosx-sdk=14.5 \\
    --target=arm64-apple-darwin \\
    main.o \\
    -dead_strip \\
    -framework Foundation \\
    -o test
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@
macosx-cross installation root.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk
Apple SDK root.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/VERSION
Selected SDK.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/VERSION/.metadata
SDK metadata.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The linker completed successfully.

.TP
.B 1
The wrapper detected an error, such as a missing target, SDK, architecture,
metadata-related configuration, or
.BR ld64.lld .

If
.B ld64.lld
itself fails, its exit status is propagated by the shell
.BR exec .
.SH NOTES
.B macosx-cross-lld
does not itself perform the final link. It configures the environment and
arguments and then replaces itself with
.BR ld64.lld .

This allows linker diagnostics and the linker exit status to be returned
directly to the caller.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ld64.lld (1),
.BR macosx-cross (1),
.BR macosx-cross-clang (1),
.BR macosx-cross-clang++ (1),
.BR macosx-cross-ldd (1)
